{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Data Parallelism.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Data Parallelism.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"data parallelism data parallelism","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Data Parallelism.md","fileName":"Data Parallelism.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Data Parallelism","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-06 22:42\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Parallel Neural Network Training]] [[.NET Data Parallelism and PLINQ]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Parallel Neural Network Training",".NET Data Parallelism and PLINQ","bigdatamanagementandprocessing.pdf","hands-onparallelprogrammingwithc8andnetcore3.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Data Parallelism.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Data Parallelism.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"data parallelism data parallelism","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Data Parallelism.md","fileName":"Data Parallelism.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Data Parallelism","heading":"Data Parallelism","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Data parallelism gives multiple workers copies of a model and different subsets of the input. Each worker calculates partial results or gradients, which are then combined to keep the model replicas consistent.\n\nThe approach scales when example-level work dominates aggregation. Synchronization and communication can become bottlenecks as worker count grows or updates become more frequent.\n\nIn .NET's Task Parallel Library, the same structural idea appears in parallel loops: a source is partitioned so workers apply one computation to different elements. Degree of parallelism, partition balance, local accumulation, and merge cost determine whether that decomposition outperforms the sequential loop.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Parallel Neural Network Training",".NET Data Parallelism and PLINQ","bigdatamanagementandprocessing.pdf","hands-onparallelprogrammingwithc8andnetcore3.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Data Parallelism.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Data Parallelism.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"data parallelism data parallelism","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Data Parallelism.md","fileName":"Data Parallelism.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Data Parallelism","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[bigdatamanagementandprocessing.pdf]]\n[[hands-onparallelprogrammingwithc8andnetcore3.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Parallel Neural Network Training",".NET Data Parallelism and PLINQ","bigdatamanagementandprocessing.pdf","hands-onparallelprogrammingwithc8andnetcore3.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}